50	tma-keep-flags-z	MAN:S8-101	TMA changes no flag (S8-101): MPR7 holds $00, P = N V and C set with Z clear, the masked P byte stays $C1 after the read of a zero byte
51	csh-length	MAN:H8-25	CSH is one byte (H8-25 map, no software-manual page): the instruction after it runs, so INX after CSH leaves X = $01
52	csl-length	MAN:H8-25	CSL is one byte (H8-25 map, no software-manual page): the instruction after it runs, so INX after CSL leaves X = $01
53	csh-csl-pair	MAN:H8-25	CSH then CSL execute and execution goes on at the next byte each time: two INX, one after each, leave X = $02
