55	st1-bypass	GUEST:ram-before-equals-ram-after	ST1 writes physical $1FE002 and does not consult the MPRs (H8-8 Table 2-2-3, S8-81, D-106): with MPR0 mapped to work RAM, RAM[2] still holds the $5B the guest wrote
56	st2-bypass	GUEST:ram-before-equals-ram-after	ST2 writes physical $1FE003 and does not consult the MPRs (H8-8 Table 2-2-3, S8-82, D-106): with MPR0 mapped to work RAM, RAM[3] still holds the $5C the guest wrote
57	st-lengths	MAN:S8-80	ST0, ST1 and ST2 are two bytes each (S8-80 to S8-82): an INX after each runs three times, and the operand $E8 (the INX opcode) is never executed, so X reads $03
